# Read Agent Entry Guide

Before making any code changes, you must read this project's `AGENTS.md` at the
dashboard project root.

`AGENTS.md` is the entry point for AI-assisted development in this project. It
explains how to follow the development documents under `docs/`.

## Required behavior

When starting a task:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` from the dashboard project root.
2. Follow the document-reading workflow defined in `AGENTS.md`.
3. Read the required project documents before editing code.
4. Do not skip the architecture spec or coding style documents when the task scope requires them.
5. Treat the coding-style completion gate in `AGENTS.md` as part of "done", not as optional background reading.
6. When integrating with a backend API, use the provider component's API contract as the source of truth; never infer API behavior from provider implementation details.
7. This component lives in the swallow monorepo as `dashboard/`; also follow the repository root `AGENTS.md` for swallow-level glossary and contract rules.
8. If `AGENTS.md` does not exist, stop and report that the project entry guide is missing.

## Important

The project rules are not defined in this Cursor rule.

This Cursor rule only requires you to start from `AGENTS.md`.

The actual source of truth for development rules, architecture rules, coding style, and API integration is defined by the project documentation referenced from `AGENTS.md`.
